    {"id":"why","type":"rectangle","x":560,"y":150,"width":720,"height":120,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e40af","backgroundColor":"#dbeafe","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":{"type":3},"seed":330040,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
    {"id":"whyt","type":"text","x":576,"y":164,"width":692,"height":92,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#1e3a8a","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":330041,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"WHY MPM / YIN, NOT FFT PEAK-PICKING\n• Locks onto the true fundamental even when overtones dominate (cello, guitar).\n• Anti-octave-error by design (MPM first-peak ≥ k·max; YIN CMNDF + threshold).\n• FFT bins too coarse: separating E2 (82.4) from F2 (87.3 Hz) needs a ~16k-pt FFT.","fontSize":13,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"WHY MPM / YIN, NOT FFT PEAK-PICKING\n• Locks onto the true fundamental even when overtones dominate (cello, guitar).\n• Anti-octave-error by design (MPM first-peak ≥ k·max; YIN CMNDF + threshold).\n• FFT bins too coarse: separating E2 (82.4) from F2 (87.3 Hz) needs a ~16k-pt FFT.","lineHeight":1.4},
    {"id":"cfg","type":"rectangle","x":560,"y":292,"width":720,"height":244,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#b45309","backgroundColor":"#fef3c7","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":{"type":3},"seed":330042,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
    {"id":"cfgt","type":"text","x":578,"y":306,"width":614,"height":216,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#7c2d12","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":330043,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"RECOMMENDED CONFIG\nSample rate        48 kHz mono float\nWindow / hop       4096 / 1024 (75% overlap)\nPre-filter         HPF ≈55 Hz + LPF ≈1300 Hz\nPrimary algorithm  MPM / NSDF (k ≈ 0.9) + parabolic interp\nAlternative        YIN / YINFFT (threshold 0.10–0.15)\nLag search         τ ∈ [36, 873] → ~55–1320 Hz\nReference          A4 = 440 Hz (configurable 432/442)\nIn-tune window     ±3–5 cents\nLibraries          TarsosDSP (JVM) · shared MPM core (KMP) · AudioKit (iOS)","fontSize":13,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"RECOMMENDED CONFIG\nSample rate        48 kHz mono float\nWindow / hop       4096 / 1024 (75% overlap)\nPre-filter         HPF ≈55 Hz + LPF ≈1300 Hz\nPrimary algorithm  MPM / NSDF (k ≈ 0.9) + parabolic interp\nAlternative        YIN / YINFFT (threshold 0.10–0.15)\nLag search         τ ∈ [36, 873] → ~55–1320 Hz\nReference          A4 = 440 Hz (configurable 432/442)\nIn-tune window     ±3–5 cents\nLibraries          TarsosDSP (JVM) · shared MPM core (KMP) · AudioKit (iOS)","lineHeight":1.5},
    {"id":"low","type":"rectangle","x":560,"y":558,"width":720,"height":104,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#c2410c","backgroundColor":"#fed7aa","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":{"type":3},"seed":330044,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false},
    {"id":"lowt","type":"text","x":576,"y":572,"width":692,"height":76,"angle":0,"strokeColor":"#7c2d12","backgroundColor":"transparent","fillStyle":"solid","strokeWidth":2,"strokeStyle":"solid","roughness":0,"opacity":100,"groupIds":[],"frameId":null,"roundness":null,"seed":330045,"version":1,"versionNonce":1,"isDeleted":false,"boundElements":[],"updated":1,"link":null,"locked":false,"text":"WHY THE WINDOW IS LARGE (the low-frequency driver)\nCello C2 = 65.4 Hz → 15.3 ms period. A stable estimate needs ~5 periods,\nso the window must be ~4096 samples. Lower notes = longer window = more latency.","fontSize":13,"fontFamily":3,"textAlign":"left","verticalAlign":"top","containerId":null,"originalText":"WHY THE WINDOW IS LARGE (the low-frequency driver)\nCello C2 = 65.4 Hz → 15.3 ms period. A stable estimate needs ~5 periods,\nso the window must be ~4096 samples. Lower notes = longer window = more latency.","lineHeight":1.4}
